      "source_line_end": 2891,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{proposition}[Upper Bounds Depend on the Ambient Order]\n\\label{prop:upper-bounds-ambient-order}\nLet $(P,\\leq)$ be a partially ordered set, and let\n$A\\subseteq S\\subseteq S'\\subseteq P$.  The upper bounds of $A$ relative to\n$S$ are exactly those upper bounds of $A$ relative to $S'$ that belong to $S$:\n\\[\n  \\{u\\in S:(\\forall a\\in A)(a\\leq u)\\}\n  =\n  S\\cap\\{u\\in S':(\\forall a\\in A)(a\\leq u)\\}.\n\\]\n\\hyperref[prf:upper-bounds-ambient-order]{Go to proof.}\n\\end{proposition}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
